[[:db/retract 17592186172425 :question/answer-fields 17592186169694] [:db/retract 17592186172425 :question/answer-fields 17592186169691] [:db/retract 17592186172425 :question/answer-fields 17592186169686] {:db/id 17592186171929 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e3db273a-c488-5a82-8422-fe1e9221beaa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171736 :question/problem "What would be a counterexample for the following false statement?\n\n$7n-2$ is even for any $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$" :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n![](images/da/da5d76e8b4ff04e99917f7b95ddaa8df9f8a8923ea39bcfcacb9667e88c577a0.svg)\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true. \n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true. \n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n![](images/51/51c76ef261110759aeec7c9ffa1eb230ae4f9ae209de324ea210c0abd476a6b6.svg)\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that $7n-2$ is odd." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171733 :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\n$2 \\mid n^2-3$ for any $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$" :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\\forall n \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\: 2 \\mid n^2-3.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\neg \\big( \\forall n \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\: 2 \\mid n^2-3\\big) \\: \\equiv \\: \\exists n \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\: 2 \\not\\mid n^2-3\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $n$ such that \n\n$$\n2 \\not\\mid n^2-3.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $n=0$ suffices:\n\nNotice that by substituting $n=0$ into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-3 & =(0)^{2}-3 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $2.$ \n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $n=0$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171737 :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\n$3q^2-2 \\gt 0$ for any $q \\in \\mathbb{Q}.$" :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\\forall q \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\: 3q^2-2 \\gt 0.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\neg \\big( \\forall q \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\: 3q^2-2 \\gt 0 \\big) \\: \\equiv \\: \\exists q \\in \\mathbb{Q}, \\: 3q^2-2 \\leq 0\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists a rational number $q$ such that \n\n$$\n3q^2-2 \\leq 0.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $q=0$ suffices:\n\nBy substituting $q=0$ into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{q}^{2}-2 & =3{(0)}^{2}-2 \\\\  & =-2 \\\\  & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $q=0$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-e3db273a-c488-5a82-8422-fe1e9221beaa" :question/id #uuid "e3db273a-c488-5a82-8422-fe1e9221beaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-221691" :question/problem "Consider the following false statement.\n\n$9n-4$ is even for any $n\\in Z$" :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀n\\in Z,\\,9n-4\\text{ is even}.\n$$\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true. \n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true. \n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n¬(∀n\\in Z,\\,9n-4\\text{ is even})\\,≡\\,∃n\\in Z,\\,9n-4\\text{ is odd}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that $9n-4$ is $\\text{odd}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-543c8dd4-cd46-5d7b-b872-28f5e756c28c" "answer-field-3aa78bb9-b187-5d4c-8bbf-7bbaca9dd68f" "answer-field-af4dda1c-b105-5306-9c38-4d8775dc52b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-543c8dd4-cd46-5d7b-b872-28f5e756c28c" :answer-field/id #uuid "543c8dd4-cd46-5d7b-b872-28f5e756c28c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-f669ffe5-88ca-5b07-91ce-5e49a9167938" :answer-field/choices ["answer-46255983-63bd-5575-a696-22f606d6b1dd" "answer-f669ffe5-88ca-5b07-91ce-5e49a9167938"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46255983-63bd-5575-a696-22f606d6b1dd" :answer/id #uuid "46255983-63bd-5575-a696-22f606d6b1dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9n-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f669ffe5-88ca-5b07-91ce-5e49a9167938" :answer/id #uuid "f669ffe5-88ca-5b07-91ce-5e49a9167938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3aa78bb9-b187-5d4c-8bbf-7bbaca9dd68f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa78bb9-b187-5d4c-8bbf-7bbaca9dd68f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-d8205af2-6ecd-55f3-8489-17a62e4ae515" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d8205af2-6ecd-55f3-8489-17a62e4ae515" "answer-84993c3c-9066-53b6-92d8-9f77ef13102d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8205af2-6ecd-55f3-8489-17a62e4ae515" :answer/id #uuid "d8205af2-6ecd-55f3-8489-17a62e4ae515" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9n-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84993c3c-9066-53b6-92d8-9f77ef13102d" :answer/id #uuid "84993c3c-9066-53b6-92d8-9f77ef13102d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-af4dda1c-b105-5306-9c38-4d8775dc52b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "af4dda1c-b105-5306-9c38-4d8775dc52b2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-cfbbb7fe-3550-5cd8-9e28-5b776f3b0385" :answer-field/choices ["answer-045b7395-71a2-554c-828d-fd5ca75abab2" "answer-cfbbb7fe-3550-5cd8-9e28-5b776f3b0385"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-045b7395-71a2-554c-828d-fd5ca75abab2" :answer/id #uuid "045b7395-71a2-554c-828d-fd5ca75abab2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "even" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfbbb7fe-3550-5cd8-9e28-5b776f3b0385" :answer/id #uuid "cfbbb7fe-3550-5cd8-9e28-5b776f3b0385" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "odd" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172425 :question/problem "Consider the following false statement.\n\n${n}^{2}-6n+8\\ge 0$ for any $n\\in N.$" :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀n\\in Z,\\,{n}^{2}-6n+8\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true. \n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true. \n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n¬(∀n\\in Z,\\,{n}^{2}-6n+8\\ge 0)\\,≡\\,∃n\\in Z,\\,{n}^{2}-6n+8<0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that \n\n$$\n{n}^{2}-6n+8<0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e15076e4-97d2-5f65-acea-378081c4d44a" "answer-field-5ea8a2d7-9fc6-5058-876a-d88758ec7e84" "answer-field-21ae7b36-dd6b-59ff-af6c-6f41d79d0ecf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e15076e4-97d2-5f65-acea-378081c4d44a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e15076e4-97d2-5f65-acea-378081c4d44a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-7b1b243b-3cfe-5281-a9ad-388d6c710076" :answer-field/choices ["answer-785be389-2c7e-5e32-bac1-d9b8c6fc0bda" "answer-7b1b243b-3cfe-5281-a9ad-388d6c710076"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-785be389-2c7e-5e32-bac1-d9b8c6fc0bda" :answer/id #uuid "785be389-2c7e-5e32-bac1-d9b8c6fc0bda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b1b243b-3cfe-5281-a9ad-388d6c710076" :answer/id #uuid "7b1b243b-3cfe-5281-a9ad-388d6c710076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{n}^{2}-6n+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5ea8a2d7-9fc6-5058-876a-d88758ec7e84" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ea8a2d7-9fc6-5058-876a-d88758ec7e84" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-fc6a3b62-d2b0-59d7-a6de-214f1bb5b3e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc6a3b62-d2b0-59d7-a6de-214f1bb5b3e7" "answer-6fd88ff2-9c21-5c96-9996-8e259a0080e2" "answer-bcef612b-10f0-5336-a6eb-34c5b1e4d0ff" "answer-96a6ebcc-0012-57b5-881e-b7398c1c2b29"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc6a3b62-d2b0-59d7-a6de-214f1bb5b3e7" :answer/id #uuid "fc6a3b62-d2b0-59d7-a6de-214f1bb5b3e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fd88ff2-9c21-5c96-9996-8e259a0080e2" :answer/id #uuid "6fd88ff2-9c21-5c96-9996-8e259a0080e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcef612b-10f0-5336-a6eb-34c5b1e4d0ff" :answer/id #uuid "bcef612b-10f0-5336-a6eb-34c5b1e4d0ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96a6ebcc-0012-57b5-881e-b7398c1c2b29" :answer/id #uuid "96a6ebcc-0012-57b5-881e-b7398c1c2b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-21ae7b36-dd6b-59ff-af6c-6f41d79d0ecf" :answer-field/id #uuid "21ae7b36-dd6b-59ff-af6c-6f41d79d0ecf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-dd07ce54-e09b-5ee5-bdef-40f6791b1af1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd07ce54-e09b-5ee5-bdef-40f6791b1af1" "answer-4760ba7c-43f4-5060-a452-2d81c2c07c7f" "answer-e4c412ad-192c-5350-b0fd-49adc6020ca4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd07ce54-e09b-5ee5-bdef-40f6791b1af1" :answer/id #uuid "dd07ce54-e09b-5ee5-bdef-40f6791b1af1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4760ba7c-43f4-5060-a452-2d81c2c07c7f" :answer/id #uuid "4760ba7c-43f4-5060-a452-2d81c2c07c7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4c412ad-192c-5350-b0fd-49adc6020ca4" :answer/id #uuid "e4c412ad-192c-5350-b0fd-49adc6020ca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173297 :tutorial/content "To **disprove** a statement means to show that it is false. In this lesson, we will learn how to disprove universal statements.\n\nSuppose we wish to disprove a universal statement of the form \n\n$$\n\\forall x \\in U, \\: P(x),\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is some universal set. To do that, we must demonstrate that the statement's negation is true. \n\nThe negation of this statement is\n\n$$\n\\neg \\big( \\forall x \\in U, \\: P(x) \\big) \\: \\equiv \\: \\exists x \\in U, \\: \\lnot P(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, to disprove a universal statement, finding one value of the variable that makes the negation true is sufficient. This value is called a **counterexample** to the original statement." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173275 :tutorial/content "For example, suppose we wish to disprove the following statement:\n\n$5n-1$ is odd for any $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$ \n\nOur statement can be written using formal notation as follows:\n![](images/d2/d22dcb4aa35870e9df2417316f7de327000f9b0cbd6758f79d4552d2a144cde1.svg)\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n![](images/32/3290200527bb59151b38e031c2b4a501784ccd6ca333bc7bef22ce5096ac6fce.svg)\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\n*To disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $n$ such that $5n-1$ is even.*\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $n=1$ suffices:\n\n*Notice that by substituting $n=1$ into the expression, we obtain*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n-1 & =5(1)-1 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*which is even.*\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\n*So, $n=1$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false.*\n\nNow that we've figured out the details, let's write down the full argument." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173298 :tutorial/content "Disprove the following statement:\n\n*$5n-1$ is odd for any $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$*\n\nCounterexample:\n\n*To disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $n$ such that $5n-1$ is even.*\n\n*Notice that by substituting $n=1$ into the expression, we obtain*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n-1 & =5(1)-1 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*which is even.*\n\n*So, $n=1$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false.*" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172195 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
